WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:03.680
When you start a long-term project like the TSA Dragster Challenge,

1
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.329
your first step is scanning the overview page to identify

2
00:00:07.329 --> 00:00:10.710
the final deliverables and organize them into 3 sprints.

3
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:12.329
On page 149,

4
00:00:12.409 --> 00:00:16.920
the overview states we must design a dragster using only specified materials.

5
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:21.329
So researching concepts and locking in material rules goes straight into sprint 1.

6
00:00:22.319 --> 00:00:24.270
Down under preliminary round check-in,

7
00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:26.799
we see what judges inspect before racing

8
00:00:27.129 --> 00:00:27.950
the completed car,

9
00:00:28.329 --> 00:00:29.809
a full-size metric drawing,

10
00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:31.670
and a printed materials list.

11
00:00:32.168 --> 00:00:32.970
Right on page one,

12
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.090
we have our roadmap.

13
00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:35.720
Blueprints in sprint 1,

14
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.439
rough fabrication and dry fit in sprint 2,

15
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.130
and final paint and documentation in sprint 3.

16
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.270
Turning to page 150,

17
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.419
we find the rules for our drawings and pre-race durability.

18
00:00:49.159 --> 00:00:52.779
Section B details the two-view metric drawing and materials list.

19
00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.080
You will sketch your initial scale design during sprint one

20
00:00:56.279 --> 00:00:59.599
and then update that final two-view drawing and materials list at

21
00:00:59.599 --> 00:01:03.080
the end of sprint 3 in case sanding changed any dimensions.

22
00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:04.309
Next,

23
00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.269
rule C warns that missing a

24
00:01:06.269 --> 00:01:09.699
single specification results in automatic disqualification.

25
00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:14.269
That means sprint 2 must include a dry fit measurement check before painting.

26
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:15.720
Finally,

27
00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.099
the race rules state no repairs are allowed after check-in,

28
00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:23.519
so sprint 3 must start with roll and string tests to catch issues early.

29
00:01:25.529 --> 00:01:27.099
On page 152,

30
00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.489
we hit the dimensional specification tables,

31
00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.540
which we sort using the exact same sprint filters.

32
00:01:33.379 --> 00:01:36.879
All rules about legal materials like the one piece body rule

33
00:01:37.059 --> 00:01:38.660
and overall dimensions for length,

34
00:01:38.779 --> 00:01:41.480
height and width get tagged in blue for sprint one.

35
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.080
These are the non-negotiables you must lock

36
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.800
into your initial sketches on sprint one.

37
00:01:47.569 --> 00:01:48.040
Next,

38
00:01:48.309 --> 00:01:49.809
the axle hole locations,

39
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:50.529
wheelbase,

40
00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:53.870
and body mass get highlighted in teal for sprint 2.

41
00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:56.360
You'll use these exact numbers when transferring

42
00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.199
your design and drilling axle holes,

43
00:01:58.449 --> 00:02:01.150
and I want dry fitting and weighing your bare wood gar.

44
00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:02.050
Meanwhile,

45
00:02:02.209 --> 00:02:03.290
rules for decals,

46
00:02:03.449 --> 00:02:04.209
washer limits,

47
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.989
and axle clips get tagged in purple for sprint 3

48
00:02:07.209 --> 00:02:08.630
during final paint and assembly.

49
00:02:11.559 --> 00:02:15.389
Page 153 covers the remaining technical tolerances.

50
00:02:15.619 --> 00:02:16.220
At the top,

51
00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.910
the power plant hole depth,

52
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:18.750
diameter,

53
00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:22.130
and 5 millimeter safety wall are non-negotiable specs.

54
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.330
You plan on paper in sprint one

55
00:02:24.509 --> 00:02:28.050
and carefully protect while shaping your wood block in sprint two.

56
00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:29.940
Under eye screws and wheels,

57
00:02:30.229 --> 00:02:32.910
making sure all four plastic wheels sit flat on the

58
00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:36.850
track and spacing eye screws at least 150 millimeters apart

59
00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:39.630
are checked during your sprint to dry fit assembly.

60
00:02:40.389 --> 00:02:41.259
For sprint 3,

61
00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:42.940
we tackle the finishing details,

62
00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.449
testing string alignment

63
00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.009
and finishing details and fixing any errors.

64
00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.020
Before building our timeline,

65
00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.630
we checked the pre-race judging rubric on pages 154

66
00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:58.369
and 155 to see how construction quality is scored.

67
00:02:58.789 --> 00:03:02.889
Notice how every pre-race rubricrow aligns with our three sprints.

68
00:03:03.229 --> 00:03:05.169
Your upfront planning in sprint one

69
00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:06.570
sets up the drawing scale,

70
00:03:06.789 --> 00:03:07.619
drawing quality,

71
00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.139
and materials list points.

72
00:03:09.429 --> 00:03:11.169
Your fabrication in sprint two

73
00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.229
covers the go no go spec check,

74
00:03:13.509 --> 00:03:14.660
body production quality,

75
00:03:14.869 --> 00:03:15.949
and vehicle assembly.

76
00:03:16.699 --> 00:03:21.220
And sprint 3 locks in body paint and finish along with your final updated drawing.

77
00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:26.059
Here is our completed 16-day sprint timeline using the 30,

78
00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:26.419
40,

79
00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.289
30 rule.

80
00:03:27.619 --> 00:03:30.699
Sprint one covers the 1st 30% on days 1 to 5.

81
00:03:30.979 --> 00:03:32.259
Research aerodynamics,

82
00:03:32.339 --> 00:03:34.059
highlight non-negotiable specs,

83
00:03:34.169 --> 00:03:38.300
and refine sketches to pass gatekeeper one before getting your wood blank.

84
00:03:38.779 --> 00:03:42.490
Sprint two takes the middle 40% from days 6 to 12,

85
00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.539
drill axle holes on day 6,

86
00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.360
rough shape on day 7 to 9,

87
00:03:46.529 --> 00:03:49.179
and dry fit and weigh on days 10 and 11.

88
00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.389
Day 12 is buffer day 1,

89
00:03:51.639 --> 00:03:56.210
giving you time to fix mistakes so your car passes gatekeeper 2 completely in spec.

90
00:03:57.039 --> 00:03:59.279
Sprint 3 covers days 13 to 16.

91
00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.639
Run roll and string tests on day 13,

92
00:04:01.839 --> 00:04:04.179
paint and assemble on days 14 and 15,

93
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.979
and use buffer day 16 to reweigh and finalize your drawing and materials list.